      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under argon (Schlenk), {Pr2(OH)(piv)5(H2O)}n (0.25 mmol per formula unit) was dehydrated under vacuum at 110 °C, dispersed in acetonitrile (2.5 mL), and treated dropwise with diethylenetriamine (150 μL, 1.4 mmol). After 30 min stirring at room temperature, 1 mL of mother liquor was mixed with 1 mL of benzene, transferred to a Λ-like glass tube, and sealed under vacuum. Slow solvent distillation over several months afforded Pr6L4·2C6H6 crystals. Yield of Ln6L4 family ca. 80%. Crystals were immersed in paraffin oil and stored at −18 °C.",
        "reagents": [
          {
            "name": "praseodymium hydroxo pivalate polymer",
